Actually, I now strongly suspect the real fix relates to the fact that the "typec" symlink is created/removed in the USB device's dir, and the correct fix is to make ucsi/typec unregister the partner BEFORE the USB host goes away, i.e., flush the connector change workqueue in the UCSI driver's remove path / on USB teardown.

